==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|urj-fin-pro|*vai}}. Probably ultimately from the same root as {{m|fi|vajaa}}, possibly by analogy with {{m|fi|tai}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{fi-pronunciation}}

===Conjunction===
{{fi-con}}

# {{lb|fi|coordinating|in question clauses}} [[or]] {{gloss|exclusive or; either what comes before or what comes after}}
#: {{ux|fi|Onko se suuri '''vai''' pieni?|Is it big '''or''' small?}}

====Usage notes====
* While it is often said that {{m|fi|tai}} is to be used in affirmative clauses and {{m|fi||vai}} is to be used in question clauses, a more precise difference is that while both can be used in question clauses, {{m|fi||tai}} is an [[inclusive or]], while {{m|fi||vai}} is an [[exclusive or]]. For instance, while {{m|fi||Söitkö sinä leivän '''tai''' hedelmät?}} and {{m|fi||Söitkö sinä leivän '''vai''' hedelmät?}} are both correct, the former asks in a yes or no question, whether you ate either bread or fruit or not, while the latter asks which you ate, the bread or the fruit.

====Derived terms====
{{col|fi
|vaiko
}}

====See also====
* {{l|fi|tai}}

===Adverb===
{{fi-adv}} {{tlb|fi|colloquial}}

# {{lb|fi|interrogative adverb}} [[is that so]]? [[or what]]?
#: {{ux|fi|Tulee '''vai'''?|Oh, [he/she/it] is coming?}}

