==Latvian==

===Etymology 1===
Borrowed from {{bor|lv|liv|vȯi}} or dialectal {{bor|lv|et|vai}}; compare other {{cog|urj-fin}} languages ({{cog|fi|vai}}, Standard {{cog|et|või}}). First found occasionally in Latvian writings in the 17th century, initially as a conjunction, then as a particle, it became more frequent in the 18th century; but only in the 19th century did it really strike root in the language.<ref name="LEV">{{R:lv:LEV}}</ref> Likely unrelated to {{noncog|sa|वा}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{lv-IPA|vài|falling}}
{{rfap|lv}}

====Conjunction====
{{head|lv|conjunction}}

# {{non-gloss|[[use]]d to [[indicate]] a [[disjunction]] [[between]] [[two]] [[element]]s}}; [[or]] {{gloss|in the [[either-or]] sense, not in the sense of [[a.k.a.]], which is {{m|lv|jeb}}}}.
#: {{ux|lv|atbildi: jā '''vai''' nē!|answer: yes '''or''' no!|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|viņa nezināja, ko pirkt: rozes '''vai''' neļķes|she didn't know what to buy: roses '''or''' carnations|inline=1}}
# {{non-gloss|[[use]]d to [[suggest]] [[vagueness]], [[uncertainty]], or a [[veiled]] [[threat]]; [[usually]] [[follow]]ed by [[ellipsis]] (...)}}; [[or]], [[or else]]...
#: {{ux|lv|ja labi grib, to darbu var veikt parasts dežurants, '''vai''' brigadieris, '''vai''' (...)|if (he) really wants, an ordinary man on duty can do this job, '''or''' a brigadier, '''or'''... ({{=}} or someone like that)|inline=1}}
#: ''vai tas kāds noziegums, kauns, '''vai'''''? — is this a crime, a shame, '''or what'''?
#: {{ux|lv|jums tas jādara, '''vai'''...|you all have to do this, '''or else'''...|inline=1}}
# {{non-gloss|[[use]]d to [[introduce]] [[conditional]] [[subordinate clause]]s}}; [[whether]], [[if]]
#: {{ux|lv|nav zināms, '''vai''' to darījis viņš|it is not known '''whether''' he did it|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|es nezinu, '''vai''' to spēšu|I don't know '''if''' I will be able to|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|pasaki, '''vai''' es esmu nodevējs|tell me '''if''' I am a traitor|inline=1}}

=====See also=====
* {{l|lv|jeb}}

====Particle====
{{head|lv|particle}}

# {{non-gloss|[[interrogative]] [[particle]], used in [[either-or]] [[question]]s}}
#: {{ux|lv|'''vai''' tu runā latviski?|do you speak Latvian?|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|lv|'''vai''' tu dzirdi?|do you hear? are you listening?|inline=1}}

====Noun====
{{lv-noun|m|-}}

# {{non-gloss|the [[word]] {{m|lv|vai}} [[itself]]; also, [[implicitly]], a [[question]]}}
#: {{ux|lv|cits pēc cita nāca tik daudzi '''vai''', ka viņa nevarēja ilgāk izturēt|so many '''vai''''s ({{=}} questions) came one after the other that she couldn't stand it any longer|inline=1}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|lv|ine-pro|*wáy|*way-|oh!, ah!; woe!, alas!}}. Cognates include {{cog|lt|vái}}, {{m|lt|vaĩ}}, {{cog|goh|wē}}, {{cog|ang|wā}}, {{cog|la|vae}}, {{cog|de|weh}}, {{cog|en|woe}}.<ref name="LEV"/>

====Pronunciation====
