==Vietnamese==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|vi|ban|q=North Central Vietnam}}

===Etymology===
Attested as Northern {{cog|mkh-mvi|ꞗĕai}}, {{m|mkh-mvi|ꞗai}} in ''Dictionarium Annamiticum Lusitanum et Latinum'' (1651), a dictionary based chiefly on the Northern dialects.

Attested in ''Phật thuyết đại báo phụ mẫu ân trọng kinh'' (佛說大報父母恩重經) as {{ltc-l|多埋}} (modern [[Sino-Vietnamese|SV]]: {{m|vi|đa}} {{m|vi|mai}}).

Compare {{cog|mkh-kat-pro|*ʔapaal||shoulder}} (whence {{cog|pac|apal}}).

Some North Central dialects have the form {{m|vi|ban}} with unlenited ‹b› (vs. mainstream form with lenited ‹v›) and ‹-n› reflex of earlier {{IPAfont|*-l}}.

